# 45 — Compose and connect creative components

**Project:** Compose and connect creative components

**Goal:** Make components composable through explicit, typed connections between their views, creative resources and backend capabilities, rather than just moving them around.

**Status:** queued

**Owner:** Unassigned

**Estimate:** TBD

**Waiting on:** owner/scope agreement; source and dependency checks

**Start:** [Astrid development skill](../../skills/astrid-dev/SKILL.md) and [shared run contract](../../skills/astrid-dev-shared/run-contract.md). [Inputs](inputs.md) · [Tasks](tasks.md). The [catalog](../index.md) owns priority, status and owner.

**Vision gaps:** [LS-003 — Compose and connect creative components](../../vision/gaps/LS-003-full-stack-contributions.md) (primary).

## Goal and scope

Make components composable through explicit, typed connections between their views, creative resources and backend capabilities, rather than just moving them around.

**Included:** Component connection and binding protocol, compatible capabilities, result transforms, typed extension hosts, user- and agent-visible attach/unbind rules, and a music-editing proof.

**Boundary:** Plan 24 owns physical layout and resizing; Plan 46 owns agent workspace actions; visual proximity never silently binds data.

## What this builds on

[Plan 24 portable/resizable components](../24-liquid-workspace/plan.md), [Plan 18 timeline](../18-timeline-editing/plan.md) and existing pack extension points. These are foundations to verify at current source revisions, not proof of a deployed result. Prefer reusing them over inventing another runtime or state owner.

## Proposed sequence

1. Specify typed resource, output and capability bindings on portable component instances.
2. Prove a timeline, preview and music beat view sharing authoritative resources with explicit time mapping.
3. Show custom frontend/backend pack contributions composing through one host contract.
4. Test incompatible binding, undo, conflicts and a genuinely different component domain.

## Interfaces and handoff

Before product work, pin actual accepted base/donor revisions, implementation owners and dependencies. Consume existing pack/component/project contracts; produce a tested contract or working artifact and link exact product PRs. Never infer authorization from a draft.

## Completion

Test incompatible binding, undo, conflicts and a genuinely different component domain. Record integrated candidate identity, real creator/agent outcomes and meaningful negative cases. Completion does not automatically close the associated vision gap.

**Authorization:** Draft, unassigned, queued. Owner decision and focused checks are required before implementation.
